0 FILE phasor-twin-control.ldr
0 Phasor Twin - Stirling phase quadrature engine CONTROL: both throws at the same phase
0 Name: model.ldr
0 Author: CrispStrobe
0 !LICENSE BSD-3-Clause : see ../licenses/phasor-twin-control.txt
0 !LDRAW_ORG Unofficial_Model
0 // Phasor Twin: two vertical crank-slider pistons, 90 deg throw phase.
0 // 40T idler on the motor output drives two 16T crank gears: both crank shafts
0 // turn the same way at 2.5x the idler; the throw phase is set by plate clocking.
0 // An externally driven kinematic Stirling-phase analogue: no gas, no heat cycle.
0 // The two pneumatic cylinders are unfitted (no hoses, no valve, no pump):
0 // they are linear guides only, so the piston law is pure crank-slider.
0 // Saved pose: throws at 135 and 225 deg, 45 deg from both dead centres.
0 // CONTROL: plate B clocked to 135 deg, the same throw phase as A.
0 STEP
0 // 01 - two floor cross members (only these two touch the floor)
